# What must never reach an image build context.
#
# Both Dockerfiles build from the repository root, so without this file every local build
# artifact is copied in. That is not merely slow: `server/Dockerfile` resolves the boot jar
# with `api/build/libs/*.jar`, and a developer who has run `./gradlew build` locally also has
# `api-0.1.0-SNAPSHOT-plain.jar` sitting there — which sorts *before* the boot jar, because `-`
# is below `.` in ASCII. The image build then fails with "no main manifest attribute".
#
# The shape of that defect is worse than the defect: it passes in CI, where the checkout is
# clean, and fails on the machine of anybody who has built the project. `docker compose up`
# working depends on what is in your build directory.

# Build output of every module, on both sides of the repo.
**/build
**/dist
**/out
.gradle
**/.gradle
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

# Generated projects and verification scratch.
verification/build
/reference/*/build

# Local and editor state.
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
**/*.iml
**/.DS_Store

# Test and coverage output.
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/*.log

# Nothing in here is needed to build an image, and some of it is large.
docs
.claude
